copygc, data/update, alloc: fix durability_keeping livelock, EC stripe copygc, and btree/wants_space churn

On pools combining replication and erasure coding (or uneven device capacities),
copygc can enter non-progressing livelocks or self-churn loops that pin
bch-copygc, keep bch2_copygc_can_make_progress() true on full devices, and
permanently stall foreground allocations and reconcile:

1. Whole-key vs per-pointer durability mismatch in data_update:
   bch2_data_update_init() and bch2_can_do_data_update() summed
   bch2_extent_ptr_durability() independently per kept pointer without device
   deduplication across stripes/replicas or online filtering, picking
   nr_replicas == 0 while bch2_extent_drop_ptrs() evaluated whole-key
   deduplicated online durability, refused to drop the pointer, committed an
   unchanged key, and returned data_update_done_no_writes_needed. Introduce
   bch2_bkey_durability_keeping() and guard bch2_extent_drop_ptrs() against
   committing unchanged keys.

2. No-op / failed evacuations counted as sectors_seen in move.c:
   Only count sectors_seen in __bch2_move_data_phys() when stats->phys is true,
   and in bch2_move_extent() when !ret, so copygc's did_work backoff triggers
   when no extents were actually moved. Also pass metadata_target rather than
   background_target when evacuating btree pointers.

3. EC stripe copygc starvation and 100%-full stripe block rejection:
   - Partially-empty EC stripes whose surviving data blocks are 100% full and
     whose empty blocks have 0 dirty sectors have alloc_lru_idx_fragmentation()
     == 0 on every block; only BCH_LRU_STRIPE_FRAGMENTATION can reclaim them.
   - bch2_copygc_get_stripe_buckets() passed time == U64_MAX to
     try_add_copygc_bucket(), but bch2_bucket_is_movable() rejected lru_idx == 0
     unconditionally, refusing to evacuate every 100%-full data block of a
     fragmented stripe. Accept movable non-empty buckets when time == U64_MAX.
   - stripe_lru_pos() scores empty_blocks + can_widen, placing tens of thousands
     of 100%-full widenable stripes at the front of BCH_LRU_STRIPE_FRAGMENTATION.
     Maintain a persistent c->copygc.ec_lru_pos cursor across copygc passes
     (wrapping at lru_end), evacuate all live blocks of each selected stripe
     together, remove the 2x penalty that excluded >=50%-full stripes whenever
     any fragmented normal bucket existed, and fall back to EC stripe copygc
     when normal bucket selection yields an empty batch.

4. Btree bucket self-churn and wants_space avoidance on reserve allocations:
   - Rewriting a btree node allocates all metadata_replicas anew. When
     non-pressured metadata devices cannot hold all metadata_replicas, skip
     >50%-full (e.g. 7/8-full) btree buckets in copygc instead of rewriting
     them back onto pressured devices and creating more 7/8-full btree buckets.
   - Order non-wants_space devices ahead of c->copygc.wants_space devices (and
     skip wants_space writepoint/partial buckets while non-pressured devices
     can satisfy remaining replicas) for >BCH_WATERMARK_normal allocations so
     copygc evacuates off pressured devices first.

5. Respect c->opts.copygc_enabled in bch2_copygc_can_make_progress().
